From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:18:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drm/msm/dpu: count only user input as idle refresh
 activity

The idle refresh rate (msm.dpu_idle_refresh_ms) returns to the mode rate
on every input event other than EV_SYN and EV_MSC. Its handler is
connected to every device with keys, relative or absolute axes, so it
also sees the event types that user space writes towards a device:
EV_LED when a compositor or logind syncs the keyboard LEDs (at every
keyboard or cover attach and keymap change), EV_SND for a beep, EV_REP
when the repeat rate is set, EV_PWR. None of them means that someone
touched the tablet, yet each one raises the rate and restarts the idle
time.

Count only EV_KEY, EV_REL, EV_ABS and EV_SW. The handler is registered
only while msm.dpu_idle_refresh_ms is set (default 0), so nothing
changes while the feature is off.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index fdcd6d48bb97..88c7c2ab4d41 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -949,11 +949,31 @@ static void dpu_idle_rr_raise(struct dpu_encoder_virt *dpu_enc)
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->kms->commit_lock[idx]);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Only events that come from the user count as activity: keys and buttons,
+ * relative and absolute axes, switches. EV_LED, EV_SND, EV_REP, EV_PWR and
+ * the force feedback types are written by user space towards the device (a
+ * compositor syncing the keyboard LEDs, a beep), and EV_SYN / EV_MSC only
+ * frame or annotate other events: none of them may raise the refresh rate.
+ */
+static bool dpu_idle_rr_input_is_activity(unsigned int type)
+{
+	switch (type) {
+	case EV_KEY:
+	case EV_REL:
+	case EV_ABS:
+	case EV_SW:
+		return true;
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
+}
+
 static void dpu_idle_rr_input_event(struct input_handle *handle,
 				    unsigned int type, unsigned int code,
 				    int value)
 {
-	if (type == EV_SYN || type == EV_MSC)
+	if (!dpu_idle_rr_input_is_activity(type))
 		return;
 
 	WRITE_ONCE(dpu_idle_rr_last_input, jiffies);
